{"Date": "04/02/2015", "Record Number": "DRCP2015-0010", "Record Type": "Design Review Committee Preliminary", "Description": "The proposed mixed-use high-rise building contains the following major components. \u2022 ground floor: hotel lobby, hotel bar/restaurant, hotel meeting room, a caf\u00e9, a full-service restaurant, retail space for Bank of America, a loading dock, parking garage entrance, and \u201cback of house\u201d functions; \u2022 floor 2: a parking garage with 89 self-parked and valet spaces, and 3 car sharing pods; \u2022 floor 3: conference space (indoor and outdoor), catering room, hotel fitness room and pool, and hotel suites with private patios; \u2022 floors 4 \u2013 12: hotel floors that typically have 28 suites per floor; \u2022 floor 13: condominiums with a shared club room, terrace open space, and other resident amenities; \u2022 floors 14 \u2013 18: residential condominiums that typically have 8 dwellings per floor with 1-, 2- and 3-bedroom units. The project has a gross floor area of 325,000 square feet and a site area of 37,739 square feet. Thus, the submitted project has a floor area ratio (FAR) of 8.63.", "Project Name": "2129 shattuck ave", "Status": "Approved", "Action": "", "Expiration Date": "", "Short Notes": "Use Permit Standard", "_cells": ["", "04/02/2015", "DRCP2015-0010", "Design Review Committee Preliminary", "The proposed mixed-use high-rise building contains the following major components. \u2022 ground floor: hotel lobby, hotel bar/restaurant, hotel meeting room, a caf\u00e9, a full-service restaurant, retail space for Bank of America, a loading dock, parking garage entrance, and \u201cback of house\u201d functions; \u2022 floor 2: a parking garage with 89 self-parked and valet spaces, and 3 car sharing pods; \u2022 floor 3: conference space (indoor and outdoor), catering room, hotel fitness room and pool, and hotel suites with private patios; \u2022 floors 4 \u2013 12: hotel floors that typically have 28 suites per floor; \u2022 floor 13: condominiums with a shared club room, terrace open space, and other resident amenities; \u2022 floors 14 \u2013 18: residential condominiums that typically have 8 dwellings per floor with 1-, 2- and 3-bedroom units. The project has a gross floor area of 325,000 square feet and a site area of 37,739 square feet. Thus, the submitted project has a floor area ratio (FAR) of 8.63.", "2129 shattuck ave", "Approved", "", "", "Use Permit Standard", "2129 SHATTUCK Ave, BERKELEY CA 94704"], "capdetail_href": "/BERKELEY/Cap/CapDetail.aspx?Module=Planning&TabName=Planning&capID1=15PLN&capID2=00000&capID3=00974&agencyCode=BERKELEY&IsToShowInspection="}
{"Date": "04/02/2015", "Record Number": "ZP2015-0071", "Record Type": "Zoning Permit", "Description": "The proposed project involves construction of a 16-floor commercial/hotel building. The ground floor would primarily consist of a new space for the Bank of America; a hotel lobby, dining room, conference room, and caf\u00e9; and a full-service restaurant. The commercial store-frontage for the Bank of America would be located on the corner of Shattuck Avenue and Center Street, oriented towards Shattuck Avenue to the west. The commercial store-frontage for the hotel and restaurant would be focused on Center Street to the south. The second floor would contain a 97-space parking garage. Floors 3 through 16 would consist of 336 hotel rooms and other hotel uses including conference rooms, as well as a terrace on the third floor with meeting space, a gym, and a pool for hotel guests.", "Project Name": "2129 Shattuck Avenue", "Status": "Approved", "Action": "", "Expiration Date": "", "Short Notes": "Use Permit Standard", "_cells": ["", "04/02/2015", "ZP2015-0071", "Zoning Permit", "The proposed project involves construction of a 16-floor commercial/hotel building. The ground floor would primarily consist of a new space for the Bank of America; a hotel lobby, dining room, conference room, and caf\u00e9; and a full-service restaurant. The commercial store-frontage for the Bank of America would be located on the corner of Shattuck Avenue and Center Street, oriented towards Shattuck Avenue to the west. The commercial store-frontage for the hotel and restaurant would be focused on Center Street to the south. The second floor would contain a 97-space parking garage. Floors 3 through 16 would consist of 336 hotel rooms and other hotel uses including conference rooms, as well as a terrace on the third floor with meeting space, a gym, and a pool for hotel guests.", "2129 Shattuck Avenue", "Approved", "", "", "Use Permit Standard", "2129 SHATTUCK Ave, BERKELEY CA 94704"], "capdetail_href": "/BERKELEY/Cap/CapDetail.aspx?Module=Planning&TabName=Planning&capID1=15PLN&capID2=00000&capID3=00944&agencyCode=BERKELEY&IsToShowInspection="}
